      "writtenOn": "2016-11-04T03:58:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also see this CL, which is relevant: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/405717/2\n\nGwendal, I think your proposal would be fine, but almost equivalent functionally to what we already have. Our host event mask will always get set before we call mkbp_send_event(), so if a non-wake event happens at almost the same time, there\u0027s some chance it will be queued before the actual EC_MKBP_EVENT_HOST event (and the host will wake). Is that a problem? I don\u0027t think so, the two events occurred at nearly the same time, it\u0027s reasonable to expect that both may remain in queue (or not).",
